                    <history>
                        <origin>
                            <origDate notBefore="1730" notAfter="1755" evidence="reign">The dating
                                is based on the supplication on <locus target="#121r"/> for the King
                                    <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5617IyasuII">ʾIyāsu II</persName> who reigned
                                from <date when="1730">1730</date> to <date when="1755">1755</date>. Therefore, the manuscript was produced around the
                                second quarter of the 18th century.</origDate>
                        </origin>
                        <provenance>Apart from the supplication for the King <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5617IyasuII">ʾIyāsu II</persName> on <locus target="#121r"/>, there are also numerous supplications for <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15522UzeftaDengel">ʿUzǝfta Dǝngǝl</persName> and his son
                                <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15523WaldaRufael">Walda Rufāʾel</persName> (e.g.,
                            on <locus target="#13r #41r #43r #45r"/>), <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15527Arsenyos">ʾArsānyos</persName> and his son <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15525WaldaMik">Walda Mikāʾel</persName> (on <locus target="#13v #15r #23r"/>) as well as <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15524WaldaKiros">Walda Kiros</persName> and his wife
                                <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15526WalattaEsrael">Walatta ʾƎsrāʾel</persName>
                            (on <locus target="#167r"/>).</provenance>
